{"explanation": "The unit is most active on a mix of classes: beetles, ticks, spiders, snails, acorns, buckeyes, espresso, chocolate sauce, cups and bowls. What they share looks like small, glossy, dark-brown or black rounded shapes, and possibly dark liquid surfaces. Within those classes, none of the photo-level properties tested reliably predicts its activity. The right-facing preference (rows 1 and 4) reversed sharply on new photos, falling to the 2nd and 6th percentiles. The fully-inside-the-frame preference (row 13) also reversed, and the right-third position effect (row 16) did not hold. So the earlier within-class patterns were most likely noise from small samples. No other row reached the unusual range in the first place. The unit is best described by its class-level preference for dark, glossy, rounded objects, not by viewpoint, framing, lighting or color within a class.", "rows": []}
```

