{"explanation": "The clearest thing about this unit is which photo classes drive it. These are small, often dark or glossy objects: beetles, ladybugs, ticks, spiders and snails; buckeyes, acorns and pomegranates; and cups, mugs and bowls of dark liquid such as espresso, consomme and chocolate sauce. Within those classes, no question in the table separates the photos reliably. The only rows at or above the 95th percentile were the facing-right preferences (rows 1 and 4). Both reversed on new photos, falling to the 2nd and 6th percentile. Row 13 (subject fully inside the frame) and row 16 (subject in the right third) also failed to replicate. The remaining rows on brightness, color tint, tilt, sharpness and subject size are all below the 95th percentile, are mostly at ordinary levels for the layer, and often rest on few photos. No within-class property can be confidently attributed to this unit.", "rows": []}
```

